(342163, 26814, 7935, '<td valign="top">nice Box Bridge  over a Bayou  good reflections and sepiatone works here        maybe cut out the bottom branches but seems a little dull      AH  infrared!!!  that''s what it is..  the white leaves    anyway a 7</td>', 'nice Box Bridge  over a Bayou  good reflections and sepiatone works here        maybe cut out the bottom branches but seems a little dull      AH  infrared!!!  that''s what it is..  the white leaves    anyway a 7', '2003-06-30 01:53:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(342165, 26289, 5767, '<td valign="top">Nice use of white here.  Great exposure, composition and lines.  Kept me interested for ahwile.  Well done.</td>', 'Nice use of white here.  Great exposure, composition and lines.  Kept me interested for ahwile.  Well done.', '2003-06-30 01:53:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(342166, 26821, 4493, '<td valign="top">This is a fine image. There isn''t much to draw in the viewer who doesn''t know who this person is. Your camera angle is a typical height and isn''t giving us a view that is unique to the occassion. The DOF chosen is very deep and doesn''t blur out the background enough to make your bride the center of the shot. The foliage being so close to her prevents a blur of the background even at a larger F/stop.  With her looking down at the flowers we are drawn to them, but with the crop and zoom you''ve chosen, there is not enough attention made to the flowers so the eye again drifts off to other parts of the image. I would have tried to use either a higher elevation for the shot, or lower angle looking up into her eyes. I''d choose a large F/stop and focus on the flowers in her hand making her face and body somewhat out of focus. The bouquet to me is the focus of the picture and I would have worked towards making the viewer appreciate the moment by using emotive elements in the capture. 5 - danny</td>', 'This is a fine image. There isn''t much to draw in the viewer who doesn''t know who this person is. Your camera angle is a typical height and isn''t giving us a view that is unique to the occassion. The DOF chosen is very deep and doesn''t blur out the background enough to make your bride the center of the shot. The foliage being so close to her prevents a blur of the background even at a larger F/stop.  With her looking down at the flowers we are drawn to them, but with the crop and zoom you''ve chosen, there is not enough attention made to the flowers so the eye again drifts off to other parts of the image. I would have tried to use either a higher elevation for the shot, or lower angle looking up into her eyes. I''d choose a large F/stop and focus on the flowers in her hand making her face and body somewhat out of focus. The bouquet to me is the focus of the picture and I would have worked towards making the viewer appreciate the moment by using emotive elements in the capture. 5 - danny', '2003-06-30 01:54:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(342167, 26631, 7935, '<td valign="top">the light is just at the wrong angle  not much can be done about that I guess    a 5</td>', 'the light is just at the wrong angle  not much can be done about that I guess    a 5', '2003-06-30 01:54:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(342168, 26424, 5767, '<td valign="top">Nice close up of this - colors and composition really make this one very interesting to look at.</td>', 'Nice close up of this - colors and composition really make this one very interesting to look at.', '2003-06-30 01:54:30.000000', NULL, 1),
