(348858, 26912, 8159, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all those who took the time to comment!<br/> <br/>I actually did experiment with a vertically-oriented crop of the barber/boy on the left... the problem was the arm of the barber on the right was still in the frame (unless I cut off the boy''s shoe), and it bothered me, so I went with this shot instead.<br/> <br/>I was backed into the corner of the barber shop and had a pretty limited area in which to shoot. Two other things were working against me in this relatively small space: the 1.6X crop factor of the 10D, and my lack of a real ultra-wide-angle lens (my widest is 24mm, or almost 39mm on the 10D).</td>', 'Thanks to all those who took the time to comment! I actually did experiment with a vertically-oriented crop of the barber/boy on the left... the problem was the arm of the barber on the right was still in the frame (unless I cut off the boy''s shoe), and it bothered me, so I went with this shot instead. I was backed into the corner of the barber shop and had a pretty limited area in which to shoot. Two other things were working against me in this relatively small space: the 1.6X crop factor of the 10D, and my lack of a real ultra-wide-angle lens (my widest is 24mm, or almost 39mm on the 10D).', '2003-07-07 09:56:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(348882, 26873, 2152, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for the comments.  This was a pretty simple setup.  The only light was from a 55 watt desk lamp with a cardboard cone I made to direct the light.  After I got the exposure down, it was just a matter of pouring the beer over and over again until I got something I wanted.  I probably took close to 75 shots.  I chose this one because I felt that the full glass shots I had lost some detail due to the dimension limits here.  I used flat beer because if I poured it straight out of the can the foam would block all the light.<br/> <br/>Outtakes:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=27704" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=27704</a> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=27703" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=27703</a></td>', 'Thanks everyone for the comments.  This was a pretty simple setup.  The only light was from a 55 watt desk lamp with a cardboard cone I made to direct the light.  After I got the exposure down, it was just a matter of pouring the beer over and over again until I got something I wanted.  I probably took close to 75 shots.  I chose this one because I felt that the full glass shots I had lost some detail due to the dimension limits here.  I used flat beer because if I poured it straight out of the can the foam would block all the light. Outtakes: //www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=27704 //www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=27703', '2003-07-07 10:32:55.000000', NULL, 0),
