(355241, 26799, 3080, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/>I think this is adorable.  The blue in her eyes doesn''t really stand out much though.  I think it does look like she was crying, and the reflection in the liquid in her eyes makes it so that the color is kind of blocked by the white of the reflection.<br/>I like the angle, and she is a really cute kid.<br/>The background has a few really bright spots from sun and I find those to be a little distracting, especially since they are near her head.  The focus and clarity are really good.  Wonderful detail.  We can see individual eye lashes.<br/>Her skin tones seem a bit red.  Either she''s had a little too much sun, her face is red from crying.  Sometimes though it''s caused by the settings on the camera.  I think it''s fixable with color adjustments in an editing program either way.<br/>I think it''s a good B shot even without the blue eyes.  Still says Baby.<br/>Good shot.<br/>~Heather~</td>', '*Critique Club*I think this is adorable.  The blue in her eyes doesn''t really stand out much though.  I think it does look like she was crying, and the reflection in the liquid in her eyes makes it so that the color is kind of blocked by the white of the reflection.I like the angle, and she is a really cute kid.The background has a few really bright spots from sun and I find those to be a little distracting, especially since they are near her head.  The focus and clarity are really good.  Wonderful detail.  We can see individual eye lashes.Her skin tones seem a bit red.  Either she''s had a little too much sun, her face is red from crying.  Sometimes though it''s caused by the settings on the camera.  I think it''s fixable with color adjustments in an editing program either way.I think it''s a good B shot even without the blue eyes.  Still says Baby.Good shot.~Heather~', '2003-07-13 15:53:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(355387, 26874, 6458, '<td valign="top">Greets from the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>And I get another of your photographs to critique - the fates must be smiling on you. I disagree with the charges that the shadows were to dark or this photo was a stretch for the challenge. I think it fits perfectly and is well exposed.<br/> <br/>I''m not a great fan of the subject matter, but technically it''s a great shot. The composition is good and the post processing is non-evident. Why doesn''t this engage me tho? I think I''d like to see more eye contact between the viewer and the rhino in back. I guess the picture feels a bit static to me. Besides that I can''t offer much criticism - sorry! <br/> <br/>Thanks for all your pics, and I can''t wait to see what you add in your profile.<br/>-Matt<br/></td>', 'Greets from the Critique Club: And I get another of your photographs to critique - the fates must be smiling on you. I disagree with the charges that the shadows were to dark or this photo was a stretch for the challenge. I think it fits perfectly and is well exposed. I''m not a great fan of the subject matter, but technically it''s a great shot. The composition is good and the post processing is non-evident. Why doesn''t this engage me tho? I think I''d like to see more eye contact between the viewer and the rhino in back. I guess the picture feels a bit static to me. Besides that I can''t offer much criticism - sorry!  Thanks for all your pics, and I can''t wait to see what you add in your profile.-Matt', '2003-07-13 21:33:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(355577, 26947, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>(Sorry I didn''t get to this during the regular "critique" week, some things came up unexpectantly).<br/> <br/>I simply love this and I suspect the parents/grandparents/guardians are looking forward to putting it on the wall.  Though his head is centered, the body going out of the lower right really gives it a dynamic feeling and gives the eyes somewhere to go.  The dof works well here to focus the attention on the boy, and not the background.  I also like the bw, and I think the softness is okay, but do think it might be interesting if you have any with sharper focus.<br/> <br/>I really can''t think of anything I would recommend to make this better, as I think it is truly effective the way it is.  Very nice work and best to you in future challenges.<br/> <br/>karmat<br/> <br/></td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat (Sorry I didn''t get to this during the regular "critique" week, some things came up unexpectantly). I simply love this and I suspect the parents/grandparents/guardians are looking forward to putting it on the wall.  Though his head is centered, the body going out of the lower right really gives it a dynamic feeling and gives the eyes somewhere to go.  The dof works well here to focus the attention on the boy, and not the background.  I also like the bw, and I think the softness is okay, but do think it might be interesting if you have any with sharper focus. I really can''t think of anything I would recommend to make this better, as I think it is truly effective the way it is.  Very nice work and best to you in future challenges. karmat ', '2003-07-14 01:34:43.000000', NULL, 0),
